 seal the tomb and restore the bones over it, ensuring no one will disturb the grave for fifty years.\"\n    28→    }\n    29→  ],\n    30→  \"characters\": [\n    31→    {\n    32→      \"id\": \"char_amontillado_1b7d65f7\",\n    33→      \"canonical_name\": \"Amontillado\",\n    34→      \"aliases\": [],\n    35→      \"role\": null,\n    36→      \"appearance\": null,\n    37→      \"personality\": null,\n    38→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    39→      \"descriptions\": [\n    40→        {\n    41→          \"text\": \"The narrator is a first-person storyteller recounting a past event involving a man named Fortunato. He claims to have purchased a pipe of Amontillado and seeks to verify its authenticity, leading Fortunato into a series of underground vaults. Throughout the narrative, the narrator maintains a calm, calculated demeanor while orchestrating a deliberate and secretive journey, culminating in a revelation that suggests a hidden, possibly fatal, intent.\",\n    42→          \"source_position\": 2046,\n    43→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    44→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    45→        }\n    46→      ],\n    47→      \"relationships\": {},\n    48→      \"evidence\": [\n    49→        {\n    50→          \"statement\": \"The narrator claims to have purchased a pipe of Amontillado\",\n    51→          \"quote\": \"I have received a pipe of what passes for Amontillado, and I have my doubts.\",\n    52→          \"position\": 2100,\n    53→          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n    54→        },\n    55→        {\n    56→          \"statement\": \"The narrator expresses doubt about the authenticity of the Amontillado\",\n    57→          \"quote\": \"I have my doubts.\",\n    58→          \"position\": 2100,\n    59→          \"confidence\": \"low\"\n    60→        },\n    61→        {\n    62→          \"statement\": \"The narrator mentions he paid the full Amontillado price without consulting Fortunato\",\n    63→          \"quote\