{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01LqYvTRMhmG619FdsAF9Wqo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me understand the root cause. The issue is that:\n\n1. **NER extraction**: SpaCy's NER tags \"Amontillado\" as a PERSON entity (since it's capitalized and appears frequently)\n2. **Validation**: The LLM validator seems to have accepted it as a character (is_valid=True)\n3. **Profile generation**: The character profiling stage generated a description for \"Amontillado\" that actually describes Montresor (the narrator)\n\nThe root cause appears to be in the **validation step** - the LLM validator should have rejected \"Amontillado\" as a non-person entity (it's a wine, not a character).\n\nLet me check if there's any mechanism to filter based on document title/metadata:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":62931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":331,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2328c887-9860-4905-a9f6-317b02fbfb9a","uuid":"74b06dae-3205-4285-9d6e-395347b9625b"}
